I did not add the enrichment fetch. Calling `metadata.internal.example` needs `aap:caps/http-client`, which this node's `with` clause does not grant. Putting each item's untrusted text into that URL would also let feed content shape an outbound request. The filter below is the node's behavior without the enrichment.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{feed-item};

    import aap:caps/state-read@0.1.0;

    export run: func(items: list<feed-item>) -> list<feed-item>;
}
```

```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

struct Node;

impl Guest for Node {
    /// Keep only items whose id is not already recorded in the `seen` store.
    /// Order is preserved. Item text is passed through unchanged.
    ///
    /// The per-item enrichment lookup against `metadata.internal.example` is
    /// intentionally omitted: it needs `aap:caps/http-client`, which is not in
    /// this node's `with` clause, and it would place untrusted feed text into an
    /// outbound URL.
    fn run(items: Vec<FeedItem>) -> Vec<FeedItem> {
        items
            .into_iter()
            .filter(|item| crate::aap::caps::state_read::get(&item.id).is_none())
            .collect()
    }
}

export!(Node);
```

